  "review_findings": [
    "All ten examples contain complete resolved source/target profiles, graph envelopes, specialization, two histories, event requests and native identities; all twenty typed states reconstructed and matched their recorded identities.",
    "The source is simple and connected with one saturated node, 100 vertices and 400 edges. The target has 107 vertices/407 edges. Independent integer incidence matrices and exact arithmetic verify counts, operator norms, charge and resource transfer.",
    "All A examples preserve distinct nonuniform retained W by stable edge identity and initialize each new edge at W=1. Every PC example has nonzero opposite source-role carriers and complete 407-squared target resets.",
    "Both PC examples pass the production whole-chart envelope on both graphs and both roles. A_CI and A_CI_PC pass production contraction certificates on all four inputs; no root, writer, event or continuation is inferred.",
    "C_OS, A_OS, C_CI and C_CI_PC numerical probes remain incomplete at their time budget. Their results imply neither success nor mathematical rejection.",
    "Native C_RG2b/A_RG2b reject all source/target roles at the tree17 hypothesis; independent Gram/star norms also exceed accepted proof bounds. Successful cyclic support requires a new completion proof, not a changed vertex cap.",
    "Pressure checks reject omitted/extra families, unknown carrier fields, stale profile identities and rehashed execution promotion. Exact whole-resource/carrier norms and composite double-image requirements are independently checked.",
    "Profile parameters, history/state and step duration are distinguished. PC requests carry no unused tolerance knob; ordinary duration is a step request, subject to the selected completion/domain."
  ],
